    {
      "id": "e89cc82653bf4dd4878469042491158b",
      "title": "Alaska Food Spoilage - Store Class Summary ",
      "url": "https://services5.arcgis.com/safXUtzLIQBW8zqM/arcgis/rest/services/Food_Spoilage_Store_Class_Summary/FeatureServer",
      "publisher": "AFPC_Admin",
      "status": "needs_review",
      "publisher_verified": false,
      "native_geography": null,
      "production_admission": false,
      "properties": {
        "snippet": "Store-level food spoilage (shrinkage) rates for rural Alaska stores by food class, month, and year, 2018–2023, developed by the UAA Institute of Social and Economic Research.",
        "extent": {
          "type": "Polygon",
          "coordinates": [
            [
              [
                -171.74419999999998,
                71.28940000000006
              ],
              [
                -131.57639999999998,
                71.28940000000006
              ],
              [
                -131.57639999999998,
                55.06170000000003
              ],
              [
                -171.74419999999998,
                55.06170000000003
              ],
              [
                -171.74419999999998,
                71.28940000000006
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        "commentsEnabled": false,
        "groupDesignations": null,
        "access": "public",
        "apiToken2ExpirationDate": -1,
        "typeKeywords": [
          "ArcGIS Server",
          "Data",
          "Feature Access",
          "Feature Service",
          "Metadata",
          "Multilayer",
          "Service",
          "Hosted Service"
        ],
        "description": "<p>This feature layer summarizes monthly food shrinkage rates for Alaska stores by product class (e.g., apples, tomatoes) and product grouping (e.g., fruits, vegetables), with stores classified by region and hub/spoke supply chain role. Includes a companion hub/spoke summary table. Approximately 47,600 records spanning January 2018 through December 2023.</p><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Developed to quantify food loss in rural Alaska supply chains and support analysis of seasonality, transportation, and supply chain factors affecting food quality and cost in remote communities.</p><p>Developed by the University of Alaska Anchorage Institute of Social and Economic Research (ISER) from store-level records, published by the Alaska Food Policy Council.</p><p><u>Variables</u></p><p>**City**&nbsp;<br />- Store location city name<br />- Example values: \"Utqiagvik\", \"Aniak\", \"Unalakleet\", \"Yakutat\"</p><p>**Lat**&nbsp;<br />- Latitude coordinate of store location<br />- Decimal degrees format<br />- Example values: 71.2894, 61.5788, 63.8789</p><p>**Lon**&nbsp;<br />- Longitude coordinate of store location<br />- Decimal degrees format (negative for West)<br />- Example values: -156.761, -159.5276, -160.7897</p><p>**STORE_REGION**<br />- Regional classification of store;&nbsp;<br />- Ex. Categories: \"North\", \"West\", \"SE-Aleutian\"</p><p>**STORE_HUBSPOKE**<br />- Main functional clustering variable for stores; based on typical supply chain characteristics<br />- Store hub/spoke classification<br />- Ex. Categories: \"Hub Air\", “Non-Hub ANC Direct Air”</p><p>**CLASS_NAME**&nbsp;<br />- Most granular category for food items&nbsp;<br />- Specific food product class<br />- Example values: \"Apples\", \"Tomatoes\"</p><p>**CLASS_NAME_GROUPING**<br />- Broader product category grouping, for nested drop down<br />- Example values: \"Fruits, basic\", “Vegetables”</p><p>**YEAR_NUMBER**&nbsp;<br />- Calendar year of observation</p><p>**MONTH_NUMBER**&nbsp;<br />- Calendar month number<br />- Range: 1-12</p><p>**Month<br />- Three-letter month abbreviation<br />- Values: \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Apr\", \"May\", \"Jun\", \"Jul\", \"Aug\", \"Sep\", \"Oct\", \"Nov\", “Dec”</p><p>**SHRINK_RATE**&nbsp;<br />- Main targeted spoilage value to display; best to average over months to show seasonality<br />- Product shrinkage rate (proportion)<br />- Decimal format representing percentage of product loss<br />- Range: 0 to ~0.8 (0% to 80%)<br />- Example values: 0, 0.031050849, 0.802550572</p><p>**N_obs**<br />- Number of observations used to calculate the shrink rate; used for Confidence interval calculations<br />- Typical values: 5 (for January data), 6 (for other months)</p><p>## Data Structure<br />- Each row represents a unique combination of: City, Product Class, Year, and Month<br />- Total observations: 47,629 rows<br />- Time period: January 2018 - December 2023<br />- Note: Some months may have missing data (e.g., January 2019 is absent in the sample data)</p><p>Dataset from UAA ISER</p>",
        "licenseInfo": "<p>Data provided by UAA ISER and the Alaska Food Policy Council for public information and planning purposes.</p>",
        "ownerId": "9e0407a865ba4ba6835d801d31f178c6",
